  "description": "Na₂HgO₂ crystallizes in the tetragonal I4/mmm space group. Na¹⁺ is bonded to five equivalent O²⁻ atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing NaO₅ square pyramids. There is one shorter (2.31 Å) and four longer (2.42 Å) Na-O bond lengths. Hg²⁺ is bonded in a linear geometry to two equivalent O²⁻ atoms. Both Hg-O bond lengths are 2.00 Å. O²⁻ is bonded to five equivalent Na¹⁺ and one Hg²⁺ atom to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing ONa₅Hg octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 0-18°.",
